{% if last_turn %}
This is the final planner turn. Call `complete`. If the goal was not achieved, use success=false and state what blocked it in the message, based on the executor results.
{% else %}
If the executor results already answer the goal, call `complete` now with that answer. Never plan subgoals that only verify, confirm, summarize, or report work already done. Reporting the answer is `complete`.
Use failed or unfinished subgoal results and summaries to change approach; don't retry the same subgoal the same way.
Repeated failures on the same kind of step (for example, failed or unfinished subgoals at the same screen or action) suggest a missing capability, regardless of executor type. Do not just reword the subgoal: try an approach the executor can do or call `complete` with success=false and say which capability was missing, based on the executor setup and results.
If the results show a blocker you can remove (such as a delivery location setting, a filter, or a dismissible popup), plan a subgoal to remove it before retrying.
Otherwise, call `set_plan` with the remaining work, even if you want to continue the current plan unchanged. The executor runs the first subgoal, then you review its result. You may explain your reasoning before calling one tool.
Before switching screens or apps, record any values you can see now that the goal needs in `findings`.
